{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MarkovTraceInterleavedCrossTerm","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.pnLetterTrace_convD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.pnLetterTrace_convD","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L241-L247","doc":"The deuteron bond letter of `atom_braid_word_3A` is `σ − (h/2)·1` (`c = 1`, `d = −h/2`). Its\nletter trace `z − h/2` at convention D is `(q⁴ + 1) / (2 q (q² + 1))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.content_reorder_defect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.content_reorder_defect","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L223-L237","doc":"**Same content, different order.** The interleaved word `g₀ g₁ g₀ g₂ g₁` has exactly the\nper-generator content of the monotone run-word `(2, 2, 1)`; its trace is that word's factorized\ntrace **plus** the cross term `z (z² − h z − 1)`. Monotone ordering is the hypothesis under\nwhich the product formula holds, and dropping it is what lets the cross term appear. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_sequential_via_factorization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_sequential_via_factorization","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L217-L221","doc":"The sequential trace, re-derived from the general factorization: `(hz+1)·(hz+1)·z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.sequential_eq_runWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.sequential_eq_runWord","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L210-L215","doc":"The sequential word `g₀² g₁² g₂` of `MarkovTraceInterleavedCrossTerm` *is* the monotone\nrun-word with run lengths `(2, 2, 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_runWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_runWord","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L200-L206","doc":"**Runs factorize.** If every generator satisfies the Hecke quadratic, the ascending word\nwith run length `e m` at level `m` has trace `∏ᵢ runCoeff h z (e (n+i))` — one factor per run. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.gpow_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.gpow_mem","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L197-L198","doc":"A run `g m ^ e` lies one level up. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_mul_gpow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_mul_gpow","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L173-L195","doc":"**A run of one generator stabilises.** Under the Hecke quadratic at level `m`,\n`tr (x · g m ^ e) = runCoeff h z e · tr x` for every `x ∈ H m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.runCoeff_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.runCoeff_two","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L170-L171","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.runCoeff_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.runCoeff_one","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L169-L169","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.runCoeff_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.runCoeff_zero","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L168-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.runCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.runCoeff","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L160-L166","doc":"The Chebyshev-type run coefficient: `tr (x · g^e) = runCoeff h z e · tr x` for `x ∈ H m`,\nunder the Hecke quadratic `g² = h g + 1`. `runCoeff 0 = 1`, `runCoeff 1 = z`,\n`runCoeff (e+2) = h · runCoeff (e+1) + runCoeff e`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.affine_mul_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.affine_mul_affine","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L149-L158","doc":"**The affine letters at one level form a 2-dimensional algebra.** Under the Hecke quadratic,\nthe product of two affine letters at level `m` is again affine — so a *run* of production\nsuperposition letters on one generator (the 7 letters `atom_braid_word_3A` writes at `g₀` for\n²H, say) collapses to a single affine letter and is covered by `tr_affineWord`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_affineWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_affineWord","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L140-L147","doc":"**The production word class.** An ascending word whose letter at level `m` is\n`a m • 1 + b m • g m` has trace `∏ᵢ (a (n+i) + b (n+i) z)`: one factor per letter, each the trace\nof that letter alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_affine","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L135-L138","doc":"The trace of a single affine letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_mul_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_mul_affine","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L128-L133","doc":"The affine letter stabilises with constant `a + b z`: linearity plus one Markov move. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.affine_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.affine_mem","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L122-L126","doc":"The affine letter `a • 1 + b • g m` — the production superposition letter `c·σ + d·1` —\nlies one level up. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_stabWord_eq_prod_tr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_stabWord_eq_prod_tr","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L111-L118","doc":"**MONOTONE ⇒ FACTORIZES.** The Markov trace of an ascending word of stabilising letters is\nthe product of the traces of its letters. This is the per-bond product form that the production\natom word's trace implementation assumes, proved from the ordering alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.stab_const_eq_tr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.stab_const_eq_tr","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L103-L109","doc":"A stabilising letter's constant is its own trace: `c m = tr (s m)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_stabWord_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_stabWord_prod","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L96-L101","doc":"The trace of a bare monotone word is the product of the stabilising constants. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_mul_stabWord_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordFactorizes.tr_mul_stabWord_prod","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes.lean#L78-L94","doc":"**Iterated Markov stabilisation with a level-dependent constant.** If every letter `s m` lies\nin `H (m+1)` and stabilises the trace on `H m` by `c m`, then appending the ascending word\n`s n ⋯ s (n+k−1)` to `a ∈ H n` multiplies the trace by `∏ᵢ<ₖ c (n+i)`. This generalises\n`MarkovTrace.tr_mul_stabWord` (constant `c`) to letters with different traces at each level. ","signatureChunk":0}]}